# Citation metadata for the AI Regulation Map dataset (Citation File Format
# 1.2.0). GitHub renders it under "Cite this repository". The DOI below is
# the Zenodo concept DOI, which always resolves to the latest weekly release;
# each release also has its own version DOI, recorded in
# public/data/release.json and quoted by the app's citations. The value is a
# placeholder until the first production release mints it: see
# docs/prds/10-dataset-doi.md, "Setup". The dataset licence (CC BY 4.0) is
# separate from the code licence (GPL-3.0, LICENSE).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, cite the version you used: each weekly release
  has its own DOI (public/data/release.json, or the Zenodo record). The DOI
  below always resolves to the latest version.
type: dataset
title: "AI Regulation Map: dataset"
authors:
  - family-names: Deane
    given-names: Ria
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
url: "https://airegulationmap.org/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/riadeane/airegulationmap"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/riadeane/airegulationmap/releases"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - AI regulation
  - AI governance
  - AI policy
  - comparative policy
  - regulatory index
abstract: >-
  Weekly snapshot of the state of AI regulation in 196 countries, scored 1
  to 5 on six dimensions (regulation status, policy lever, governance type,
  actor involvement, enforcement level, and a maturity index), with
  per-country descriptions, key legislation, source URLs, research
  confidence, the sub-indicator audit trail behind every score, and the full
  score history. Scores are assigned by an automated research pipeline
  against a fixed rubric and re-run weekly; the methodology and its limits
  are documented at https://airegulationmap.org/methodology.html.
